  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "Where each flake falls, the whiteout puffs and the frost shape vary per cast. The 620 ms telegraph and the storm window stay fixed so players can learn to dodge it."
  },
  "director_notes": "Boss-weight area storm for a top-down camera. Choices: (1) a 620 ms pulsing frost telegraph sized exactly to the 2.2-unit storm zone, so it's fair; (2) the storm is three stacked snow layers (big tumbling flakes, fine fast snow, hard sleet streaks) falling over the whole zone (sparks emit_radius_px) and slanted by the wind (wind_px), with low whiteout and ground drift for the top view; (3) frost grows to the edge of the circle and outlasts the storm. Sound is mostly wind, rising, gusting and dying, with a thin icy hiss."
}
